        "scope": "Literal ordinary-tree universal Delete-only Hall. Restricted deletion faces remain separate."
      },
      {
        "claim_key": "E993-C3-G1-POINTWISE-ADDABILITY-BOUND",
        "status": "REFUTED",
        "statement": "For every full ordinary G1 tuple with i_r(U)>0, every independent r-set S of U has at most r addable vertices.",
        "scope": "Literal full ordinary G1 scope at r=p-2; universal over all independent r-sets in each residual. r29 Cycle 1 (2026-09-25) scope note: distinct from the r29 high-tail keys: the registered refutation witnesses fail 3p \u2265 2\u03b1 + 1 (a theorem given E993-BIPARTITE-LEAF-HIGH-TAIL-POINTWISE, not a data check); E993-BIPARTITE-TAGGED-SHADOW-BOUND is a size-restricted incidence count whose constants k and 2(a \u2212 k) are incomparable with the refuted per-set bound. Status REFUTED unchanged."
      },
      {
        "claim_key": "E993-LOWER-REGION-ORDINARY-FAVORABLE-LEAF-AGGREGATE",
        "status": "OPEN",
        "statement": "For every finite ordinary tree T with a=alpha(T), first strict descent x(T) of its integer zero-extended independence counts, and natural p satisfying x(T)+2<=p and 3p<2a+1, the complete sum over original leaves v with Delta_p(T-v)<0 of Delta_(p-1)(T-{v,s_v})-Delta_(p-1)(T-N_T[s_v]) is nonpositive.",
        "scope": "Connected acyclic finite simple graphs; original leaves are distinct tags even when supports coincide; original supports and original closed neighborhoods; empty selected set has sum zero; no residual hypothesis; no governed RTree transport."
      },
      {
        "claim_key": "E993-LOWER-REGION-TWO-FOR-ONE-WEIGHTED-HALL",
        "status": "OPEN",
        "statement": "For every finite ordinary tree T and natural p with x(T)+2<=p and 3p<2alpha(T)+1, fix F={original leaves v: Delta_p(T-v)<0}. For each independent B define w_F(B)=#{v in F intersect B: (N_T(s_v) intersect (B minus {v})) is nonempty}. The capacitated bipartite graph from independent (p+1)-sets B with supply w_F(B) to independent p-sets D with capacity w_F(D), with an edge exactly when D=B minus {q} for q in B or D=(B minus (N_T(s) intersect B)) union {s} for s notin B with exactly two neighbors in B, has an integral flow saturating every upper supply.",
        "scope": "Ordinary trees only; fixed strict original selector and original supports; all clone pairs over each allowed set pair are permitted. A sufficient mechanism for the lower-region aggregate, not equivalent to its scalar assertion. Distinct from the refuted literal Delete/Retag and deletion-only mechanisms because their clone compatibility and edge sets differ. No governed RTree assertion."
      },
      {
        "claim_key": "E993-LOWER-REGION-EARLY-MARKED-OCCUPANCY-TRANSFER",
        "status": "OPEN",
        "statement": "For every finite ordinary tree T, natural p with x(T)+2<=p and 3p<2alpha(T)+1, fix the original strict selector F={degree-one leaves v: Delta_p(T-v)<0} and original supports s_v. Put k=p-1, H_v=T-{v,s_v}, W_v=N_T(s_v) minus {v}, q_v(k)=#{independent k-sets of H_v meeting W_v}, Q=sum_F q_v(k), and E=sum_F sum_{A independent k-set of H_v meeting W_v} #{vertices of H_v addable to A}. Then i_x(T)*E <= (x+1)*i_(x+1)(T)*Q.",
        "scope": "Universal CT_x premise itself, not the already established conditional implication. All selected tags counted separately, zero-extended coefficients; i_x>0 on the guard. Distinct from refuted pointwise addability, same-rank covariance shortcut, and governed RTree assertions."
      },
      {
        "claim_key": "E993-LOWER-REGION-PER-LEAF-DOWN-MAP-INJECTIVITY",
        "status": "REFUTED",
        "statement": "For every finite ordinary tree T and natural p with x(T)+2<=p and 3p<2alpha(T)+1, and every original leaf v with Delta_p(T-v)<0, the rational linear map d_p from the vector space on marked independent p-sets of H_v=T-{v,s_v} to the space on marked independent (p-1)-sets, sending each basis set to the sum of its one-vertex deletions still meeting W_v=N_T(s_v) minus {v}, is injective.",
        "scope": "Universal LOCAL per-selected-leaf operator, distinct from any operator mixing tags or the scalar aggregate. Mechanism refutation by selected T22 arm dimensions."
      },
      {
        "claim_key": "E993-LOWER-REGION-SAME-RANK-WEIGHTED-OCCUPANCY-DOMINATION",
